# Coin toss — incremental workflow

Follow this order on every task. Do not skip steps.

## Scope of changes

- **Visual improvements:** Change only what the request targets (CSS, one component, one animation). Do **not** rewrite the whole game, restructure files, or refactor unrelated code.
- **Features:** Do **not** add new mechanics, UI, or polish until the **core coin toss** looks and feels right (flip, landing, feedback, timing).

## Before major changes

- Ensure there is a **known-good Git commit** (or ask the user to commit) before large or risky edits.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs over one big replacement.

## Test before moving on

- After each round of changes, **verify the coin toss in the browser** (or describe what the user should check if you cannot run it).
- Repeat the same core flow several times (toss → result → reset) before starting the **next** feature or visual pass.
- Fix regressions from the current round before adding anything new.

## When in doubt

- Smallest change that satisfies the request.
- One concern per change set.
- Ask before expanding scope beyond what was requested.
